    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147-a1">

                <pb facs="0251" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg167"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: In your polite note of the 24th of
                    April last, your excellency was pleased to inform me, in accordance with the
                    instructions of your Government, that all that referring to the cancellation of
                    the actual shares of the Panama Canal and Railroad companies, was included in
                    the convention between Colombia and the United States, signed on the 22d of
                    January last, for the opening of the canal.</p>
                <p>I shall be obliged by your excellency’s telling me, as early as possible, if
                    modifications, which, according to the final part of the note referred to, are
                    considered as violating the Spooner law, are only those which concern the
                    concessions of each of the companies, or if they are such also as may be adopted
                    with regard to the (treaty itself) convention spoken of.</p>
                <p>With this motive, etc.,</p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Luis Carlos
                    Rico.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To his excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. M. Beaupré</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary of
                            the United States, etc.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
